From d5ebde445068874054a8afc9e57e71f4dc994b18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:03:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ui: Mode Ladder, its line on the FORMAT row, mode
 controls follow the ladder

Why: on the camera screen the operator must see which resolution the
ladder runs and must not be offered mode controls that Core refuses.

What: bridge properties fpsTakeMax, ladderEnabled, ladderActive,
ladderRung, ladderCount and ladderText from Core's state; the FORMAT row
shows Core's running line (wrapping inside its column); the FPS picker
stops at fps_take_max in a take; resolution, crop, bit depth and
compression controls are disabled while the ladder is active; a Mode
Ladder switch in Settings shows Core's reason when it is refused;
set_fps and set_mode_ladder get the 10 s reply time; applyFps shows the
FPS Core accepted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T93jucKMhWYnQM1yyFVkbH
